From: Muhammad Waleed Badar <walid.badar@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drivers: sdhc: esp32: make the input delay phase configurable

The ESP32-S3 SDMMC host samples the data lines with a programmable
delay phase (sdmmc_ll_set_din_delay_phase). The driver programs phase 0
once at init and never touches it again, which is only right for
default speed. ESP-IDF exposes the phase per slot (sdmmc_slot_config_t
delayphase) because boards whose slot goes through the GPIO matrix need
a later sampling point at 40 MHz. Add a Kconfig option for the phase
used in high speed mode and apply it whenever the card clock changes.

Signed-off-by: Muhammad Waleed Badar <walid.badar@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/sdhc/Kconfig.esp32 | 10 ++++++++++
 drivers/sdhc/sdhc_esp32.c  | 14 ++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 24 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/sdhc/Kconfig.esp32 b/drivers/sdhc/Kconfig.esp32
--- a/drivers/sdhc/Kconfig.esp32
+++ b/drivers/sdhc/Kconfig.esp32
@@ -14,6 +14,16 @@ config SDHC_ESP32
 	  SDHC driver for Espressif ESP32 SoCs. Supports SD, SDIO and MMC
 	  cards through the SD/MMC host controller.
 
+config SDHC_ESP32_HS_DIN_DELAY_PHASE
+	int "Input delay phase in high speed mode (40 MHz)"
+	default 0
+	range 0 3
+	depends on SDHC_ESP32
+	help
+	  Delay phase used to sample the data lines once the card clock is
+	  in high speed mode. Phase 0 samples at the clock edge; boards whose
+	  slot is routed through the GPIO matrix often need phase 1 or 2.
+
 config SDHC_BUFFER_ALIGNMENT
 	default DCACHE_LINE_SIZE if DCACHE
 	default 4
